  message: "SATISFIED on the filed instance in PR #2033 (dev fa70fb3680; lab /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/saruf_11032026/RESULT.md). Owner ruling 2026-11-03: ADR-0043 s4 'minted only for endpoints that SURVIVE filtering' stands; the tier filter drops an edge when either endpoint is a node it removed (symmetric with the dst rule) and the shape predicate is gone. Behavioural evidence, the item's own repro re-run: knex surveyed base (cd6aeed541, worktree) vs branch: the four external_symbol SOURCE nodes (lib/dialects/index.js file + getDialectByNameOrAlias, two path spellings) and all 42 edges leaving them are gone, zero external_symbol sources remain, no edge with a real source node removed, nothing dangling; a --max-tier 4 survey ties all 42 to knex's two tier-4 nodes. Self: 38 edges from scip_pb2.py and three vendored parser.c stand-ins gone. caddy: byte-identical. Gates: test_phase_de_reorder G2 (pb2 edges GONE, JS min.js arm), test_max_tier membership + reaching fixture. NOT ASSERTED: the general clause 'no external_symbol is ever minted for the SOURCE of an edge an in-tree file emitted' -- a no-node source still gets a stand-in (ADR-0037 synthesis), and on self one such edge comes from requirements.py's hand-built 'requirements:<path>' src id, filed as its own item from this batch."  # 4357
